Phase 1 — IAM Hardening
Goal

Secure identities and stop account takeover.

AWS Services
IAM
MFA
AWS Organizations (optional)
Steps
1. Create IAM Admin User
IAM → Users → Create User

Create:

SecurityAdmin

Attach:

AdministratorAccess

Why:

Never use root account daily.
2. Enable MFA
IAM → Users → SecurityAdmin
→ Security Credentials
→ Assign MFA

Use:

Google Authenticator
Microsoft Authenticator

Why:

Prevent password-only compromise.
3. Create Security Group
IAM → Groups

Example:

CloudSecurityTeam

Attach policies.

Why:

Easier permission management.
4. Enable Password Policy
IAM → Account Settings

Require:

12+ characters
Uppercase
Lowercase
Numbers
Symbols

Why:

Reduce weak passwords.
